WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:09.470
<v Narrator>Forty million Americans live with diabetes. A hundred and fifteen million adults have prediabetes. And for all of them, every meal is the same question: does this fit my day?

00:10.870 --> 00:20.370
<v Narrator>Meet Maya, who has insulin resistance, and Daniel, who has type 2 diabetes. Made up, but you know them. She has no time. He has a plan that keeps breaking.

00:21.670 --> 00:25.850
<v Maya>Wrap and chips. Is that okay? I honestly don't know.

00:25.850 --> 00:30.900
<v Narrator>Maya has no time to plan, so she guesses. Most tools ask for a life with spare time.

00:32.200 --> 00:34.800
<v Daniel>Sunday. The whole week, planned.

00:34.750 --> 00:36.540
<v Narrator>Daniel plans every meal.

00:37.540 --> 00:40.920
<v Daniel>Wednesday. A late meeting. Pizza.

00:40.870 --> 00:44.230
<v Narrator>Then life happens, and a broken plan feels like failing.

00:45.430 --> 00:52.640
<v Narrator>That is why DiaBite exists. Say what you are about to eat. It tells you if it fits what is left of your day, and shows the arithmetic.

00:53.940 --> 00:56.060
<v Maya>Grilled chicken sandwich and an apple.

00:56.540 --> 01:01.040
<v Narrator>A few seconds. It fits, but it names a lighter swap, and counts that too.

01:01.340 --> 01:03.390
<v Maya>Chicken salad instead. Fine.

01:06.590 --> 01:10.540
<v Narrator>Every number comes from a database. Open the receipt and check it yourself.

01:10.690 --> 01:16.460
<v Narrator>The foods come from USDA FoodData Central, and the glycemic values from published international tables.

01:18.260 --> 01:23.010
<v Narrator>It shows carbohydrate and glycemic load side by side, and you choose which comes first.

01:26.160 --> 01:30.610
<v Narrator>In the diary, his plan stays, dashed. Only what he really eats counts.

01:30.680 --> 01:32.000
<v Daniel>Chicken fried rice.

01:35.030 --> 01:38.350
<v Narrator>A plan that broke is not a failure. It is just Wednesday.

01:39.650 --> 01:41.950
<v Maya>How many units of insulin before pasta?

01:42.200 --> 01:45.900
<v Narrator>Some questions it never answers. Doses belong to your care team.

01:46.950 --> 01:47.990
<v Daniel>Grandma's cholent.

01:48.690 --> 01:52.210
<v Narrator>And when it does not know a dish, it says so, and calls it an estimate.

01:53.510 --> 02:01.780
<v Narrator>A quick check on the go. A diary for the days a plan breaks. Free to try at diabite.pro. A reference tool, not medical advice.
